WEBVTT

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.446
Half a century ago,

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.307
futurists started predicting
the rise of remote work.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.046
In 1993, management guru
Peter Drucker wrote

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:11.266
that commuting to an office is obsolete.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.076
But a quarter-century later,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.283
nearly half of global companies
still weren't allowing remote work at all.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.668
Not anymore.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.276
Around the world, many companies
are now requiring remote work.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.616
This forced remote work has amplified
many of the challenges we had

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.570
when we worked face-to-face.

00:04:29.594 --> 00:04:33.136
And even in that hard-to-imagine future
beyond the pandemic,